# Edge OS — ShellCheck Configuration
#
# Controls: enable/disable checks, set severity thresholds
# Reference: https://github.com/koalaman/shellcheck/wiki

# ─── Severity ───
# Minimum severity to report (error, warning, info, style)
# Disable: no minimum (show all)

# ─── Disable specific checks ───

# SC1091: "Not following" — for sourced files we don't have in context
disable=SC1091

# SC1090: "Can't follow non-constant source" — for dynamic sourcing
disable=SC1090

# SC2154: "Variable is referenced but not assigned" — for sourced variables
disable=SC2154

# SC2034: "Variable appears unused" — for arrays/purpose-built variables
disable=SC2034

# SC2086: "Double quote to prevent globbing" — when intentional
# We keep this ENABLED — it finds important bugs. Exceptions handled inline.

# SC2181: "Check exit code directly" — when using $? is clearer
# We keep this ENABLED — best practice to check commands directly.

# ─── Enable additional checks ───
# enable=all  # Too noisy — use selective enables

# ─── Shell selection ───
# shell=bash  # Most Edge OS scripts are bash
